NAME
    more - page through text a screenful at a time

SYNOPSIS
    more [file ...]

DESCRIPTION
    Shows the files named, as one stream (globs expand, "-" is the
    console), 23 lines at a time. After each 23 lines it prints
    --More-- and waits for a key, read from the console without echo;
    the prompt is wiped once the key comes. more is /BIN/MORE.

    Keys at the --More-- prompt:
        space   the next page
        Enter   one more line
        q, Q    quit (so does Ctrl-D, the end of console input)
        other   the next page

    With no file both the text and the keys come from the console, so
    `more` alone is only a curiosity until Y1/OS has pipes.

LIMITS
    Up to 24 names in all, after glob expansion.

EXAMPLES
    more /DOCS/PORT.MD       a long file (md renders it better)
    more /MAN/C*             the pages starting with C, one after
                             another

NOTES
    On the instruction-level emulator a lower-case q is read as end of
    input, which quits as well.
    Removed from the P8X version: paging a pipe (dir -R | more).
    New: several files, globs and "-". The pager itself is shared with
    man and md (see pager).
    Ported from P8X os/commands/more.c 2026-09-23.

SEE ALSO
    pager, man, md, cat, head, tail
